.svg) are\n\n- ![](images/63/6301e767c6538ae4707f3d93ff4d0529778a836ff128e64cb0fa828369ef583d.svg) for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ![](images/35/35c129770db807490a09631057c0eba23bfa465775b7c3cbfec4feae2bce478a.svg) ![](images/05/053c53695c9135de14fbf7f1107641b09bc58e3f64ab77189037b79f6202aeff.svg) for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- ![](images/c7/c728504bb72e8cf919ccdce83ec6cfa72bc5e8e15ea8dfac671088ddcf2a36c5.svg) ![](images/05/053c53695c9135de14fbf7f1107641b09bc58e3f64ab77189037b79f6202aeff.svg) for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the ![](images/0c/0cf2eee0cdec31b7acdc244a255aaee7d6d520cfeee67b64ac9cf215f5377477.svg)th sine coefficient of ![](images/03/035f3a0cae1ed2af1401d897d6289c9c0c64a2d0901b0d2a2584cc39e9305e0c.svg) is ![](images/5e/5e342d421e8368686e21a1427e476d20fc14cba1333b005526a49d082953338d.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229175 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c24953c9-584d-5ff1-a2f7-1addba6f623e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-236925ac-8f18-52a6-be78-880a69837dd3" :question/id #uuid "236925ac-8f18-52a6-be78-880a69837dd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-340767" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $5\\text{th}$ Fourier sine coefficient of $4f(x)-g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $4f(x)-g(x)$ are\n\n- $4{a}_{0}-{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $4{a}_{n}-{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $4{b}_{n}-{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $5$th sine coefficient of $4f(x)-g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n4{b}_{5}-{d}_{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f6ce8e2c-2c01-51f1-9dd8-1153184ac72a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6ce8e2c-2c01-51f1-9dd8-1153184ac72a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ce8e2c-2c01-51f1-9dd8-1153184ac72a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-095dc636-bcdf-5389-b4b4-076c56cdab36" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49155e74-8a92-55f9-995f-33bf99cd888c" "answer-0de381fb-0d5d-57af-ad50-d5c06db2cc49" "answer-aa52fabc-721d-5494-a7ec-39f7def4aa2e" "answer-61203ab7-ae3c-52ad-81b4-3fedd3b1f4c6" "answer-095dc636-bcdf-5389-b4b4-076c56cdab36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49155e74-8a92-55f9-995f-33bf99cd888c" :answer/id #uuid "49155e74-8a92-55f9-995f-33bf99cd888c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{a}_{0}-{c}_{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0de381fb-0d5d-57af-ad50-d5c06db2cc49" :answer/id #uuid "0de381fb-0d5d-57af-ad50-d5c06db2cc49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{a}_{5}-{c}_{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa52fabc-721d-5494-a7ec-39f7def4aa2e" :answer/id #uuid "aa52fabc-721d-5494-a7ec-39f7def4aa2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{b}_{0}-{