\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the {{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-023c4211-a889-5d42-9272-5f4138514c0f" "answer-field-5f2568e6-9bf3-59d7-85fc-c8b637d02d62"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-023c4211-a889-5d42-9272-5f4138514c0f" :answer-field/id #uuid "023c4211-a889-5d42-9272-5f4138514c0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-17745f27-8937-5357-92fc-8ff4e50016de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-17745f27-8937-5357-92fc-8ff4e50016de" "answer-59f1c3e0-a00a-5b17-833b-f276d32ff27a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17745f27-8937-5357-92fc-8ff4e50016de" :answer/id #uuid "17745f27-8937-5357-92fc-8ff4e50016de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59f1c3e0-a00a-5b17-833b-f276d32ff27a" :answer/id #uuid "59f1c3e0-a00a-5b17-833b-f276d32ff27a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f2568e6-9bf3-59d7-85fc-c8b637d02d62" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f2568e6-9bf3-59d7-85fc-c8b637d02d62" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-753420fa-eadc-5316-991d-15deacaa93c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f797e43f-749c-5178-812e-513c4f32b37f" "answer-753420fa-eadc-5316-991d-15deacaa93c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f797e43f-749c-5178-812e-513c4f32b37f" :answer/id #uuid "f797e43f-749c-5178-812e-513c4f32b37f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-753420fa-eadc-5316-991d-15deacaa93c2" :answer/id #uuid "753420fa-eadc-5316-991d-15deacaa93c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "sine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186315023 :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-{x}^{2}$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the {{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d3147fbb-19de-5c4b-b748-97469c2e48ab" "answer-field-dbc432da-5bad-5417-aa50-f365fc5f282b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d3147fbb-19de-5c4b-b748-97469c2e48ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3147fbb-19de-5c4b-b748-97469c2e48ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-eb413bb7-fd7f-5122-8467-8a7725efd86e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb413bb7-fd7f-5122-8467-8a7725efd86e" "answer-9a79c998-d6a9-5b0d-af34-2b6334cc9b11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb413bb7-fd7f-5122-8467-8a7725efd86e" :answer/id #uuid "eb413bb7-fd7f-5122-8467-8a7725efd86e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a79c998-d6a9-5b0d-af34-2b6334cc9b11" :answer/id #uuid "9a79c998-d6a9-5b0d-af34-2b6334cc9b11" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dbc432da-5bad-5417-aa50-f365fc5f282b" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbc432da-5bad-5417-aa50-f365fc5f282b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-258e0488-ebe5-5f57-9c9c-c40c1259cf50" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8b493ca6-f359-5fab-b573-1e46e9d4e5cf" "answer-258e0488-ebe5-5f57-9c9c-c40c1259cf50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b493ca6-f359-5fab-b573-1e46e9d4e5cf" :answer/id #uuid "8b493ca6-f359-5fab-b573-1e46e9d4e5cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-258e0488-ebe5-5f57-9c9c-c40c1259cf50" :answer/id #uuid "258e0488-ebe5-5f57-9c9c-c40c1259cf50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "sine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c24953c9-584d-5ff1-a2f7-1addba6f623e" :question/id #uuid "c24953c9-584d-5ff1-a2f7-1addba6f623e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340804" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a09ceeba-ecb8-5b78-8ce8-e6874d799d16" "answer-field-d76d84f8-75b1-5fcc-a0e9-e6b5f26f9e73"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a09ceeba-ecb8-5b78-8ce8-e6874d799d16" :answer-field/id #uuid "a09ceeba-ecb8-5b78-8ce8-e6874d799d16" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e02047fa-7a6d-56bd-b2df-24d20ad221c8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b09cfbad-f0db-5e18-adb8-e9efb3c1a68b" "answer-e02047fa-7a6d-56bd-b2df-24d20ad221c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b09cfbad-f0db-5e18-adb8-e9efb3c1a68b" :answer/id #uuid "b09cfbad-f0db-5e18-adb8-e9efb3c1a68b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e02047fa-7a6d-56bd-b2df-24d20ad221c8" :answer/id #uuid "e02047fa-7a6d-56bd-b2df-24d20ad221c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d76d84f8-75b1-5fcc-a0e9-e6b5f26f9e73" :answer-field/id #uuid "d76d84f8-75b1-5fcc-a0e9-e6b5f26f9e73" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-cd915d82-c5ec-5f1c-a803-f4ed4253c4c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd915d82-c5ec-5f1c-a803-f4ed4253c4c0" "answer-15bd2080-99a9-51ae-89ba-6e5bbd200ba9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd915d82-c5ec-5f1c-a803-f4ed4253c4c0" :answer/id #uuid "cd915d82-c5ec-5f1c-a803-f4ed4253c4c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15bd2080-99a9-51ae-89ba-6e5bbd200ba9" :answer/id #uuid "15bd2080-99a9-51ae-89ba-6e5bbd200ba9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "sine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229718 :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=-5{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the {{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To check whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =-5(-x)^{4}+2(-x)^{2} \\\\  & =-5{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2} \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ we have that $f$ is even.\n\nFor the Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is even and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd, so $f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${b}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{even}$ and the $\\text{sine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-31c42783-a0bc-5aa4-9ecd-25d720e96f18" "answer-field-144e708f-bce4-5aa2-882e-202cff09afa5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-31c42783-a0bc-5aa4-9ecd-25d720e96f18" :answer-field/id #uuid "31c42783-a0bc-5aa4-9ecd-25d720e96f18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-5b3b4336-5434-516f-a61d-246576df1308" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b3b4336-5434-516f-a61d-246576df1308" "answer-aa7e0c03-665a-5c7b-a616-a0d332659fe8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b3b4336-5434-516f-a61d-246576df1308" :answer/id #uuid "5b3b4336-5434-516f-a61d-246576df1308" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa7e0c03-665a-5c7b-a616-a0d332659fe8" :answer/id #uuid "aa7e0c03-665a-5c7b-a616-a0d332659fe8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-144e708f-bce4-5aa2-882e-202cff09afa5" :answer-field/id #uuid "144e708f-bce4-5aa2-882e-202cff09afa5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-78347118-a192-5bee-b58d-939c8d82936e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7d8d0820-748e-505c-93fc-afe0435abb62" "answer-78347118-a192-5bee-b58d-939c8d82936e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d8d0820-748e-505c-93fc-afe0435abb62" :answer/id #uuid "7d8d0820-748e-505c-93fc-afe0435abb62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78347118-a192-5bee-b58d-939c8d82936e" :answer/id #uuid "78347118-a192-5bee-b58d-939c8d82936e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "sine terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230213 :tutorial/content "In applications, we often build new periodic signals by adding old ones together or scaling their amplitudes.\nThe Fourier series behaves well under these transformations, i.e., scaling and adding functions simply scales and adds their Fourier coefficients.\n\nMore precisely, let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi$-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor constants $\\alpha$ and $\\beta,$ define\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x).\n$$\n\nThen $h$ is also $2\\pi$-periodic, and its Fourier series has the form\n\n$$\nh(x)\\sim \\dfrac{A_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\big(A_n\\cos(nx)+B_n\\sin(nx)\\big),\n$$\n\nwhere the coefficients are obtained by combining the coefficients term-by-term:\n\n- $A_0=\\alpha a_0+\\beta c_0$\n\n- $A_n=\\alpha a_n+\\beta c_n$ for $n\\ge 1$\n\n- $B_n=\\alpha b_n+\\beta d_n$ for $n\\ge 1$\n\nEquivalently,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)\n\\sim\n\\dfrac{\\alpha a_0+\\beta c_0}{2}\n+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\Big((\\alpha a_n+\\beta c_n)\\cos(nx)+(\\alpha b_n+\\beta d_n)\\sin(nx)\\Big).\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** In this notation, \n\n- the *constant Fourier coefficient* is $A_0,$ while\n\n- the *term* in the series is $\\dfrac{A_0}{2}.$\n\nLet's see a concrete example below." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229265 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
